---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { cv, formatPeriod } from "../lib/cv";
import profile from "../assets/profile.jpeg";
---

<Base
  title="About · Mustafa Ekrem Kenter"
  description="Digital Lab Lead at Turkish Technology. The arc: chatbots since 2018, LLM products since 2023, enterprise MCP in production today."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-14">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">
      The research scout boat ahead of a very big ship.
    </h1>

    <div class="prose-mek mt-8">
      <Image
        src={profile}
        alt="Mustafa Ekrem Kenter"
        width={224}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        class="rounded-full float-right ml-6 mb-2 size-24 sm:size-28 object-cover border border-line"
      />
      <p>
        I lead the Digital Lab at Turkish Technology, the research team that
        scouts ahead of Turkish Airlines. Our job is to explore emerging
        technologies and turn the promising ones into things the airline
        actually ships.
      </p>
      <p>
        The clearest example: we built one of the first enterprise MCP
        platforms in the world, connecting an airline's core services (flight
        search, booking, baggage, city guides) directly to AI assistants,
        with interactive branded cards rendered inside the chat. It made
        Turkish Airlines one of the first airlines live on both ChatGPT and
        Claude. One backend, one tool spec, every major AI agent.
      </p>
      <h2>The shift I write and speak about</h2>
      <p>
        Booking engines are moving from forms to conversations. Full-page web
        is giving way to chat-native UI. Distribution is becoming a question
        of which capabilities you expose, not which channel you own. Recent
        talks: the keynote at Future of Aviation 2026 in Helsinki (<em
          >"Chat Is the New Booking Engine"</em
        >) and <em>"Building Chat-Native UI with MCP Apps"</em> at AWS's Twin
        Strikers event in Istanbul.
      </p>
      <h2>Before this role</h2>
      <p>
        Seventeen years across the stack. CTO at Popupsmart, where we shipped
        LiveChatAI in under two months. Lead engineer at BlueReceipt. A
        government-funded startup of my own. And earlier years at Turkish
        Airlines building Boti (the airline's chatbot, live on WhatsApp and
        Messenger years before LLMs made conversation easy) and leading the
        mobile app's cloud migration to AWS. Earlier still: ad engines serving
        150M requests a day, and anti-money-laundering systems for Turkey's
        Financial Investigation Unit.
      </p>
      <p>
        That mix of founder instincts inside an airline headed for 100 million
        passengers a year is what the Digital Lab runs on. Along the way
        I've led teams in every setting there is: a fully remote US startup,
        my own company, and now a lab inside one of the world's biggest
        airlines. I've come to care as much about growing engineers as
        shipping with them.
      </p>
      <h2>Beyond work</h2>
      <p>
        I'm a father of two, and my wife's support is the quiet infrastructure
        behind everything above. I give seminars on communication and
        relationships, an interest in humans that turns out to be
        surprisingly useful in engineering leadership.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're working on agentic AI, MCP, or airline retailing, I take a
        small number of advisory conversations and speaking invitations:
        <a href={cv.profile.booking} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >book 15 minutes</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="eyebrow">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="mt-5 border-l border-line">
        {
          cv.experience.map((e) => (
            <li class="relative pl-6 pb-8 last:pb-0">
              <span class="absolute -left-[5px] top-1.5 size-2.5 rounded-full bg-accent" />
              <p class="font-mono text-xs text-faint">{formatPeriod(e)}</p>
              <h3 class="font-semibold mt-1">
                {e.role} · <span class="text-soft font-normal">{e.company}</span>
              </h3>
              {e.summary && <p class="text-sm text-soft mt-1">{e.summary}</p>}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <a href="/cv/" class="link inline-block mt-6 text-sm">Full CV →</a>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
